  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Viet Nam Floods</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The moderate to strong La Ni&#xF1;a weather event which has developed in the Pacific Ocean is resulting in increased seasonal rains, particularly in S.E. Asia, where current heavy rainfall and typhoons are expected to continue into November. 
&#xA0;
From the beginning of October, the Lower Mekong region has experienced prolonged, heavy rains that have caused severe and widespread flooding and landslides in several provinces of Vietnam and Cambodia and parts of Lao PDR and Thailand. 
&#xA0;
This widespread flooding as left millions of people feeling the impacts of a deadly double disaster as they are faced with the worst floods for decades as well as the compounding impact of the ongoing Covid-19 pandemic.</narrative>
  </description>
